        <head>ST. HELENS.</head>
        <p>ST. HELENS.</p>
        <p>ST. HELENS YOUTH'S CE.</p>
        <p>Fred Nlolloy, the St. Helens youth who was rrested on a charge of stealing a purse and remanded in con- sequence of a communication from the medical otficer at Walton Gaol, WU brought up again at the the local police court on Saturday. Dr. Cotton certified that the youth was mentally deficient, and that his tendencies were of a criminal nature. He was sect to the work- house with a view to being removed to an asylum. ST. HELENS CATHOLIC CHARITY BALL. The seventy-first annual Catholic charity ball was bold at St. Helens Town Hall on Wednesday night. There was a large 'attendance, and the assembly room and other parts of the building were most attractively arranged. The function was under the patronage of the Mayor and all the local 'gentry. Mr. Arthur A. 'Slater again filled the &amp;lice of hon. secretary, and he and the committee have in years gone by raised large sums in aid of the local charities. Mr. E. Clayton's band provided the music, and Mr. 11-Alwagen was the caterer.</p>
      </div>
