        <p>the ordinary consumer, for the man in the street or his wife does not directly buy leather, Leather is bought by the boot and shoe manufacturers, saddlery and harness makers, upholsterers, 1.14 g and trunk makers, purse makers, belting makers, and other manufacturers These trades, which use leather as a raw material, employ far more men than the leather making trades, and they would be injured by dearer leather.</p>
