        <p>COUNTY PALATINE OF CHESTER. ISOLATION HOSPITALS ACTS, 1893 AND 1901. CONSUMPTIVE SANITORIUM. NTOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that a Committee II appointed by the County Council of the County of Chester under the above Acts will, at the Crewe Arms Hotel,Crewe, on MONDAY,the 30th day of March, 1908, at 11 o'clock in the Forenoon,hold a PUBLIC INQUIRY, as to the necessity for the establishment of a Hospital for the Treatment of Pulmonary Tuberculosis, and as to the proper Site for the same, and the District or Districts for which such Hospital should be established. AND NOTICE IS HEREBY FURTHER GIVEN, that at such Inquiry any Persons interested may attend and state their case before the said Committee. Dated this 26th day of February, 1908. REGISALD POTTS, Clerk to the Cheshire County Council.</p>
        <p>LIVERPOOL WINTER ASSIZES, FEBRUARY, 1908. The Commissions for holding these Assizes will be opened at Liverpool, on Saturday, the 29th February. The Court will sit on Monday, the 2nd March, at 11 o'clock a.m., and on every other day during the Assizes at 10.30 o'clock a.m. unless otherwise directed. The Prosecutors aiid Witnesses in the aftermentioned cases are required to be in attendance at the times specified in the following List,and not earlier; and on all subject days, at the sitting of the Court; and the trials are to proceed in the order in which the cases are arranged in the List, unless the Court shall otherwise direct, viz. : On MONDAY, the 2nd March, at 11 o'clock, a.m. The King versus John Byrne, murder; Albert Korff and another, conspiracy; Simeon Isaac Lord, forgery : Charles Connor, wilful neglect of children ; John Murphy and another, criminal assault; Isaac Grayson, wounding ; Georgina Hillhouse and another, bigamy ; Doctor Harold, libel ; William Cox, criminal assault ; John Golding, wounding ; Walter Smith, burglary ; John Stewart, criminal assault ; John William Cobb, larceny of a post letter • Arthur Simkins, bigamy ; Sarah Martin, abortion ; John Miles Sumner, burglary ; Mary McDowall, wounding ; Herbert Richardson, false pretences ; Arthur Clarke and others, using a place for betting ; Richard Body, bigamy ; Mary Elizabeth Wilcock, larceny; James Rafferty, warehouse-breaking; Peter Dunn, perjury ; Peter Vogt, housebreaking ; Thomas Boyd, housebreaking ; George Stanley Wilson, larceny; William Henry Shay, wounding ; William Little, shopbreaking ; Frank Pattison and others, ware- house breaking. e. 4041 And all Other Cases. All Indictments settled by Counsel must be forwarded to me Engrossed and Abstracted. The foregoing Regulations will be strictly enforced, and persons making default in the observance of them will be liable to have their costs disallowed. HERBERT STEPHEN, Clerk of Assize. Office of Clerk of Assize, Preston, 26th February, 1908. N.B.—lt is particularly requested that all Deposi- tions, Inquisitions, and Recognisances may be immedi- ately forwarded to me at Preston.</p>
